Win-Slate (this repository; formerly slate-for-windows)

Win-Slate 1.0.0 — a self-contained Windows executable build and installer
for Slate, derivative work of Slate under Apache-2.0. This is a recompile /
host port based on Sam Wasserman's work; it is not an official Wasserman
release and is offered WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND (see Apache-2.0
Sections 7–8 and the project README).

Repository: https://github.com/ChrisToast89/Win-Slate

- App host: Go + Wails (instead of Electron) for a native Windows binary
- Installer: per-user Setup that audits dependencies, installs/updates the
  app, and optionally helps install Claude Code for the AI brain

Generative coding tools were used to assist the Windows port, installer,
and packaging. Credit for the original product belongs with
Sam Wasserman.

